    "command": "npm run test:php-wasm-recursive-generated && npm run test:php-wasm-recursive-packages",
    "scope": "Original PHP-Wasm npm/runtime archives and Composer ZIPs preserve recursive callbacks and owned closures on ordinary-source and reviewed-IR paths. Authors are removed before source-free execution; deterministic compiler-free reassembly and installed-file hashes remain unchanged. Base and mixed packages pass 48 Node runs across embedded, Composer and bundled APIs, startup/lazy loading and weak/strict PHP. Sixteen Chromium arrangements each repeat in two fresh contexts. Base callers pass 1130 checks and 388 rejections; mixed callers pass 1249 checks including all nineteen primitive families and sixteen-argument Unit callbacks. Exact Lean/PHP documentation compiles and executes through Composer. Separate actual wasm32 probes cover allocation failures, closure capacity/reuse, uint64 generations, invalid callback contexts, active close, context exhaustion, Zend longjmp/exit recovery and 952 partial-construction aborts. Nested reply owners are checked before Lean copies; premature-release and missing-retirement mutants fail at named checks, not Wasm traps. Original copied and acyclic callable packages pass again.",
